{"absent":["Boot-time stall-suppression predicate and runtime suppress flag storage and ownership.","Tracepoint string wrapper purpose and ftrace dump mode values.","Fanout and level-count defaults and numeric range of hierarchy depth.","Locking and concurrency rules for segmented-list operations beyond node raw-lock wrappers.","Grace-period sequence object layout and completion-value meanings.","Segment identifiers and total segment count semantics."],"dossier":"D02","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_stall_is_suppressed.alt_1","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_stall_is_suppressed.alt_2","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_ftrace_dump_stall_suppress.alt_1","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_ftrace_dump_stall_unsuppress.alt_1","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_ftrace_dump_stall_suppress.alt_2","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_ftrace_dump_stall_unsuppress.alt_2"],"text":"Stall suppression is reported as active when either a boot-time condition holds or a runtime suppress flag is set in one configuration, and only from the boot-time condition in the other configuration where the runtime suppress and unsuppress operations are inert."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_ftrace_dump"],"text":"A diagnostic dump helper performs at most one dump per call site using a one-time guard, disabling tracing around the dump and bracketing it with stall suppress and unsuppress operations."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_init_levelspread","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_fanout_exact","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_fanout_leaf"],"text":"Level spread initialization either uses an exact mode where the leaf level takes a configured leaf value and higher levels take a configured fanout value, or a computed mode where each level spread is derived from CPU count and per-level node counts with rounding up."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_first_leaf_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_is_leaf_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_is_last_leaf_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::_rcu_for_each_node_breadth_first","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_for_each_node_breadth_first","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::srcu_for_each_node_breadth_first","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_for_each_leaf_node"],"text":"Hierarchy traversal exposes leaf detection by comparing node level against the configured depth, last-leaf detection by address comparison against the final node, breadth-first iteration over the node array, and leaf-only iteration starting at the first leaf."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::for_each_leaf_node_possible_cpu","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_find_next_bit","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::for_each_leaf_node_cpu_mask"],"text":"Per-CPU leaf iteration walks either possible CPUs bounded by a leaf node group range or set bits of a caller mask translated into the same group range."},{"kind":"lock","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_lock_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_unlock_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_lock_irq_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_unlock_irq_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_lock_irqsave_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_unlock_irqrestore_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_trylock_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_spin_trylock_irqsave_rcu_node","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::raw_lockdep_assert_held_rcu_node"],"text":"RCU node locking is done through wrappers around a node-private raw lock with plain, interrupt-disabling, interrupt-saving, and trylock forms; acquisition adds an acquire-side ordering barrier and release paths assert interrupts are disabled."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_gp_is_normal","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_gp_is_expedited","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_async_should_hurry","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_expedite_gp","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_unexpedite_gp","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_async_hurry","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_async_relax","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_cpu_online","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_cpu_beenfullyonline"],"text":"This configuration reports grace periods as always normal and never expedited, asynchronous hurry as never needed, expedite and hurry operations as inert, and every CPU as online and fully online."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::RCU_SCHEDULER_INACTIVE","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::RCU_SCHEDULER_INIT","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::RCU_SCHEDULER_RUNNING"],"text":"Scheduler state values are inactive zero, init one, and running two."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcutorture_type"],"text":"Torture flavor enumeration distinguishes classic, tasks, tasks-rude, tasks-tracing, trivial, sleepable, and invalid flavors."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcutorture_get_gp_data","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::do_trace_rcu_torture_read","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_gp_set_torture_wait","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_set_gpwrap_lag","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_get_gpwrap_count","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::srcutorture_get_gp_data","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_watching_zero_in_eqs","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_get_gp_seq","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_exp_batches_completed","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_force_quiescent_state","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_check_boost_fail","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::show_rcu_gp_kthreads","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_get_gp_kthreads_prio","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_fwd_progress_check","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_gp_slow_register","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_gp_slow_unregister","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::srcu_batches_completed","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::show_rcu_tasks_gp_kthreads","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::tasks_cblist_init_generic","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::show_rcu_tasks_classic_gp_kthread","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::show_rcu_tasks_rude_gp_kthread","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_bind_current_to_nocb","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_is_task_rcu_boosted","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_stall_notifier_call_chain","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_get_jiffies_lazy_flush","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::rcu_set_jiffies_lazy_flush"],"text":"Torture and observability helpers in these fragments are neutral defaults: zeroed flags and sequence outputs, inert waits and lag settings, no callback, zero batch counts, no force or forward-progress action, inert slow-path registration, and fixed boost and priority answers."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_init","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_enqueue","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_init","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_get_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_n_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_test_flags"],"text":"A plain callback list holds a head pointer, a tail link pointer, and a length. A segmented list holds a head pointer plus per-segment tail links, per-segment grace-period sequence values, per-segment lengths, a total length, and flags."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_init","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_enqueue","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_flush_enqueue","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_cblist_dequeue"],"text":"Plain callback list operations initialize an empty list, append at the tail with length increment, transfer a whole source list into a destination optionally leaving one entry behind, and remove from the head with length decrement and tail reset when emptied."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_set_len","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_add_len","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_inc_len","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_get_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_set_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_add_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_move_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_inc_seglen","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_n_segment_cbs"],"text":"Segmented-list accounting keeps a total length and independent per-segment lengths with set, add, increment, and move operations; moving between distinct segments transfers the source count and zeroes the source, and same-segment or empty-source moves do nothing."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_init","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_disable","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_set_flags","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_clear_flags","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_is_enabled","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_test_flags","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_empty","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_n_cbs"],"text":"Segmented-list lifecycle initializes all tails to the head with zero counts and an enabled flag, and disable clears enabled after warning if callbacks remain; flags support set, clear, test, and enabled query."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_ready_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_pend_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_restempty","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.h::rcu_segcblist_segempty","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_first_cb","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_first_pend_cb","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_nextgp"],"text":"Readiness means enabled with a non-empty done segment, pending means enabled with a non-empty remainder after done, segment emptiness is determined by tail-pointer equality with a special head comparison for done, and first-entry accessors return null when disabled."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_enqueue","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_entrain"],"text":"New callbacks are appended to the newest segment with count updates, while entrain attaches to the newest non-done occupied segment when any callback exists and extends later segment tails to the new entry."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_extract_done_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_extract_pend_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_insert_count","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_insert_done_cbs","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_insert_pend_cbs"],"text":"Extraction moves either the ready prefix or the pending suffix into a plain list and repairs segment tails and counts; insertion performs the reverse transfer for counts, done prefix at the head, or pending suffix at the newest tail, and empty sources do nothing."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_advance","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_advance_compact"],"text":"Advancement checks waiting segments in order against completed grace-period state, folds each completed segment into the done segment, then compacts by collapsing vacated tails and shifting later segments and their sequence values downward."},{"kind":"export","sids":["kernel/rcu/tree.c::poll_state_synchronize_rcu_full","kernel/rcu/tree.c::poll_state_synchronize_rcu_full_unordered","kernel/rcu/tree.c::rcu_get_root"],"text":"Grace-period polling reports completion when either the normal or expedited tracked state is marked completed or the corresponding global sequence has passed the tracked value, with an ordered form bracketing the unordered check with barriers."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["kernel/rcu/rcu.h::for_each_leaf_node_possible_cpu","kernel/rcu/rcu.h::for_each_leaf_node_cpu_mask","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_disable","kernel/rcu/rcu_segcblist.c::rcu_segcblist_advance"],"text":"Leaf-scoped iteration warns when given a non-leaf node, and segmented-list disable warns when invoked with callbacks still queued."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::WRITE_ONCE"],"text":"External dependency owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/rwonce.h::READ_ONCE"],"text":"External dependency owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_mb.alt_1"],"text":"External dependency owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_mb.alt_2"],"text":"External dependency owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_1"],"text":"External dependency owned by another dossier."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/asm-generic/bug.h::WARN_ON_ONCE.alt_2"],"t